rephrased_query:
Complaint under Section 321 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita 2023 (BNS) - Causing grievous hurt by dangerous weapons or means - against unknown person(s).

Pursuant to Section 2 of the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam 2023 (BSA), the complainant seeks production of any evidence that may be relevant to the incident, including but not limited to:

- Any eyewitness accounts or statements;
- Physical traces of the altercation;
- Medical reports regarding the injuries sustained by the victim;
- Security footage or any other form of visual evidence;
- Any other relevant information or material that may aid in the investigation.

Furthermore, the complainant requests that the investigating officer exercise their powers as per Section 59 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita 2023 (BNSS) to identify and apprehend the perpetrator(s) of the alleged offense, and to conduct a thorough investigation to establish the facts of the case as per Section 159 of the BNSS.
